/*  What a function stores into what it was given — `src/Interpreter/TypeChecker.Stores.cs`
    (docs/SOUNDNESS.md, obligation O4).

    ★ Inside a body every parameter has depth 0, and so does everything the body makes. Neither is
    true where the function is CAST: what it makes lies in the region open at the cast, and what it
    is given can lie anywhere outside that. So a store between the two is written down in the body,
    as a PAIR, and judged at each cast, where both depths are known — after every body has been
    checked, so that a function cast above its own `Bind` is held to the same rule.

    ★ A place in a pair is a number: a parameter's slot from 0, -1 for the object a method is
    cast on, -2 for something the body makes, and -3 and below for a name the body CAPTURED — its
    rabbit depth where the body was written (-3 - place), or the parameter it is there
    (-1000001 - place), or -2147483648 when nothing can say.

    ★ C# hangs what a function stores on its type. Here it is kept under a KEY: `name@line` for a
    function, `owner's name` for a method, `lambda@row:column` for one with no name,
    `interface<tab>name<tab>method` for one reached through an interface. A name that holds a
    function with no name is pointed at that function's key by `held`.

    ⚠ Every set of places is walked in ascending order, and so is every list of pairs: which pair
    is met first decides which refusal is given, and C# gives the same one.
*/

Pull a book on collections.
    Define object store-pair with (the number from-place, the number into-place).
    Define object store-relay with (the number slot, the text toward, the number toward-position).
    Define object store-note with (the node value, the node target, the number line,
        the series of number sources, the series of number targets).
    Define object store-pass with (the number slot, the text handed).
    Define object call-note with (the text callee, the text display, the series of node handed-args, the node receiver,
        the series of number given-depths, the series of fact given-holds, the number receiver-depth,
        the number call-depth, the number line, the number within,
        the series of number given-sources, the series of number receiver-sources,
        the series of store-pass passes).
    Define object store-frame with (the text summary, the fact setter, the node body,
        the map from text to number positions, the series of number referenced,
        the map from text to number captured, the number parent,
        the series of store-note stores, the series of number calls).
    Define object function-value with (the text stored-as, the text name, the number line, the number column).
    Define object parameter-value with (the text owner, the number slot, the number line, the number column).

    /// Everything the rule keeps for the length of one check. Each part is a series or a map, so a
    /// copy of the book still reaches the one set of them.
    Define object store-book with (
        the series of store-frame frames,
        the series of number closed,
        the map from number to fact traced,
        the map from text to series of store-pair pairs,
        the map from text to fact known,
        the map from text to fact captures,
        the map from text to number defined-in,
        the map from text to series of number wild,
        the map from text to series of store-relay relays,
        the series of call-note calls,
        the series of function-value values,
        the series of parameter-value parameter-values,
        the map from text to fact taken-back,
        the map from text to text held).

    Bind store-book to fresh-store-book:
        Return a new store-book {
            the frames a series of store-frame,
            the closed a series of number,
            the traced a map from number to fact,
            the pairs a map from text to series of store-pair,
            the known a map from text to fact,
            the captures a map from text to fact,
            the defined-in a map from text to number,
            the wild a map from text to series of number,
            the relays a map from text to series of store-relay,
            the calls a series of call-note,
            the values a series of function-value,
            the parameter-values a series of parameter-value,
            the taken-back a map from text to fact,
            the held a map from text to text }.
    Done.

    // ── Places ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    Bind number to outer-unknown:
        Return -2147483648.
    Done.

    Bind number to outer-parameter-base:
        Return -1000001.
    Done.

    /// The place a captured name at this rabbit depth has in a pair.
    Bind number to outer-code, given (the number depth):
        If depth is cast captured-parameter-depth, return cast outer-unknown.
        Return -3 - depth.
    Done.

    Bind fact to is-outer, given (the number place):
        Return place is less than -2.
    Done.

    Bind fact to is-outer-parameter, given (the number place):
        Return place is less than cast outer-parameter-base + 2 and place is not cast outer-unknown.
    Done.

    /// The rabbit depth a captured place has in the body it was captured from.
    Bind number to outer-depth, given (the number place):
        If cast is-outer-parameter on (place), return 0.
        Return -3 - place.
    Done.

    /// The same numbers, smallest first.
    Bind series of number to places-in-order, given (the series of number numbers):
        Define sorted-out as a series of number.
        Define taken as a series of fact.
        For each one-number in numbers, repeat:
            Insert false into taken.
        Done.
        Define round as 0.
        While round is less than the number of numbers, repeat:
            Increment round by 1.
            Define best as 0.
            Define spot as 0.
            While spot is less than the number of numbers, repeat:
                Increment spot by 1.
                If item spot of taken is false:
                    If best is 0, the best becomes spot.
                    Otherwise if item spot of numbers is less than item best of numbers, the best becomes spot.
                Done.
            Done.
            Insert item best of numbers into sorted-out.
            Item best of taken becomes true.
        Done.
        Return sorted-out.
    Done.

    /// The same pairs, by where they come from and then by where they go.
    Bind series of store-pair to pairs-in-order, given (the series of store-pair listed-pairs):
        Define sorted-out as a series of store-pair.
        Define taken as a series of fact.
        For each one-pair in listed-pairs, repeat:
            Insert false into taken.
        Done.
        Define round as 0.
        While round is less than the number of listed-pairs, repeat:
            Increment round by 1.
            Define best as 0.
            Define spot as 0.
            While spot is less than the number of listed-pairs, repeat:
                Increment spot by 1.
                If item spot of taken is false:
                    If best is 0, the best becomes spot.
                    Otherwise:
                        Define this-pair as item spot of listed-pairs.
                        Define leading as item best of listed-pairs.
                        If this-pair's from-place is less than leading's from-place, the best becomes spot.
                        Otherwise if this-pair's from-place is leading's from-place and this-pair's into-place is less than leading's into-place:
                            The best becomes spot.
                        Done.
                    Done.
                Done.
            Done.
            Insert item best of listed-pairs into sorted-out.
            Item best of taken becomes true.
        Done.
        Return sorted-out.
    Done.

    Bind fact to holds-pair, given (the series of store-pair listed-pairs, the number from-place, the number into-place):
        For each one-pair in listed-pairs, repeat:
            If one-pair's from-place is from-place and one-pair's into-place is into-place, return true.
        Done.
        Return false.
    Done.

    // ── Frames ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// The names a body written inside another can reach that are not its own, each with its
    /// rabbit depth there — a parameter's is the one that says "nothing can say".
    Bind map from text to number to captured-names, given (the series of map from text to binding enclosing):
        Define names as a map from text to number.
        For each scope in enclosing, repeat:
            For each pair in scope, repeat:
                Define held as the value of pair.
                If held's shape's kind is not "FunctionType" and held's permanent is false:
                    If held's parameter, in names, the entry for (the key of pair) becomes cast captured-parameter-depth.
                    Otherwise, in names, the entry for (the key of pair) becomes held's depth.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
        Return names.
    Done.

    /// Begins a body. `summary` is the key its pairs go under, or "" for a body no cast can ask;
    /// `parameters` is a list of `[<type> <name>]`; `reached` is what `captured-names` gave, or
    /// an empty map for a body that captures nothing. Gives back the frame to go back to.
    Bind number to open-store-frame unto checker, given (the text summary, the fact setter, the node body,
            the node parameters, the fact with-receiver, the map from text to number reached):
        Define positions as a map from text to number.
        Define referenced as a series of number.
        Define index as 0.
        For each parameter in parameters's children, repeat:
            Define taken as cast one's resolved on (cast field-of on (parameter, 1)).
            In positions, the entry for cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (parameter, 2)) becomes index.
            If cast is-reference-type on (taken) or taken's kind is "InterfaceType", insert index into referenced.
            Increment index by 1.
        Done.
        If with-receiver:
            In positions, the entry for "one" becomes -1.
            Insert -1 into referenced.
        Done.
        Define around as one's store-now.
        Define captured as a map from text to number.
        For each pair in reached, repeat:
            Define name as the key of pair.
            // A parameter hides a captured name it shares a spelling with.
            If (the entry for name in positions) is void:
                Define placed-as as cast outer-code on (the value of pair).
                If around is greater than 0:
                    Define outside as item around of one's stores's frames.
                    Define there as the entry for name in outside's positions.
                    // What the body around this one captured was counted somewhere further out still.
                    If (the entry for name in outside's captured) is not void, the placed-as becomes cast outer-unknown.
                    Otherwise if there is not void, the placed-as becomes cast outer-parameter-base - there.
                Done.
                In captured, the entry for name becomes placed-as.
            Done.
        Done.
        If summary is not "":
            In one's stores's defined-in, the entry for summary becomes around.
            In one's stores's captures, the entry for summary becomes the size of captured is greater than 0.
            If (the entry for summary in one's stores's pairs) is void:
                In one's stores's pairs, the entry for summary becomes a series of store-pair.
                In one's stores's wild, the entry for summary becomes a series of number.
                In one's stores's relays, the entry for summary becomes a series of store-relay.
            Done.
        Done.
        Insert (a new store-frame { the summary summary, the setter setter, the body body, the positions positions,
            the referenced referenced, the captured captured, the parent around,
            the stores a series of store-note, the calls a series of number }) into one's stores's frames.
        The one's store-now becomes the number of one's stores's frames.
        Return around.
    Done.

    /// Ends a body whose check went through, and goes back to the one around it.
    Bind void to close-store-frame unto checker, given (the number around):
        Define index as one's store-now.
        Define frame as item index of one's stores's frames.
        // A body written inside another is traced NOW, while the names it captured and the
        // functions bound beside it are still in scope. A top-level body waits, and is traced only
        // if asked.
        If frame's parent is greater than 0 or the size of frame's captured is greater than 0, cast one's trace-frame on (index).
        If frame's summary is not "", in one's stores's known, the entry for frame's summary becomes true.
        Insert index into one's stores's closed.
        The one's store-now becomes around.
    Done.

    /// Where each side of every store and every argument of every cast in a body can come from.
    Bind void to trace-frame unto checker, given (the number index):
        If (the entry for index in one's stores's traced) is not void, return.
        In one's stores's traced, the entry for index becomes true.
        Define frame as item index of one's stores's frames.
        If the number of frame's stores is 0 and the number of frame's calls is 0, return.
        // What the walk makes on the way goes with this rabbit; the places are numbers, and stay.
        Pull a rabbit.
            Define gathered as a series of node.
            Cast gather-depth-nodes on (frame's body, gathered).
            Define locals as cast one's local-depths on (gathered, frame's positions, frame's referenced, frame's captured, true).
            For each store in frame's stores, repeat:
                For each place in cast one's symbolic-depth on (store's value, frame's positions, frame's referenced, locals, frame's captured, true), repeat:
                    Insert place into store's sources.
                Done.
                For each place in cast one's symbolic-depth on (store's target, frame's positions, frame's referenced, locals, frame's captured, true), repeat:
                    Insert place into store's targets.
                Done.
            Done.
            For each call-index in frame's calls, repeat:
                Define noted as item call-index of one's stores's calls.
                // One flat run of numbers: each argument's places, then the mark that ends them.
                // ⚠ Not a series of series: one made inside this rabbit would go with it, and the
                // compiler written in Cufet cannot yet build an object that holds one.
                For each argument in noted's handed-args, repeat:
                    For each place in cast one's symbolic-depth on (argument, frame's positions, frame's referenced, locals, frame's captured, true), repeat:
                        Insert place into noted's given-sources.
                    Done.
                    Insert cast sources-end into noted's given-sources.
                Done.
                If cast is-none on (noted's receiver) is false:
                    For each place in cast one's symbolic-depth on (noted's receiver, frame's positions, frame's referenced, locals, frame's captured, true), repeat:
                        Insert place into noted's receiver-sources.
                    Done.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.

    // ── What is written down as a body is checked ─────────────────────────

    /// Whether a value of this type carries a series or a map: itself, or inside it.
    Bind fact to holds-container unto checker, given (the node shape):
        Define kind as shape's kind.
        If kind is "SeriesType" or kind is "MapType" or kind is "MatrixType" or kind is "ChannelType" or kind is "AddressType", return true.
        If kind is "ObjectType", return cast one's object-holds-container on (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (shape, 1)), a map from text to fact).
        Return false.
    Done.

    Bind fact to object-holds-container unto checker, given (the text name, the map from text to fact seen):
        // The registered type, since one that was merely written carries no fields.
        Define definition as cast one's definition-of on (name).
        If definition is void, return true.
        If (the entry for name in seen) is not void, return false.
        In seen, the entry for name becomes true.
        Define embedded as cast embedded-name on (definition).
        If embedded is not "":
            If cast one's object-holds-container on (embedded, seen), return true.
        Done.
        For each positional in (cast field-of on (definition, 2))'s children, repeat:
            If cast one's field-holds-container on (positional, seen), return true.
        Done.
        For each pair in (cast field-of on (definition, 3))'s children, repeat:
            If cast one's field-holds-container on (item 2 of pair's children, seen), return true.
        Done.
        Return false.
    Done.

    Bind fact to field-holds-container unto checker, given (the node shape, the map from text to fact seen):
        Define kind as shape's kind.
        If kind is "NumberType" or kind is "BitsType" or kind is "FactType" or kind is "VoidType" or kind is "TextType", return false.
        If cast is-nothing on (shape) or kind is "none", return false.
        If kind is "ObjectType", return cast one's object-holds-container on (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (shape, 1)), seen).
        If kind is "RecordType":
            For each part in (cast field-of on (shape, 1))'s children, repeat:
                If cast one's field-holds-container on (part, seen), return true.
            Done.
            For each pair in (cast field-of on (shape, 2))'s children, repeat:
                If cast one's field-holds-container on (item 2 of pair's children, seen), return true.
            Done.
            Return false.
        Done.
        If kind is "VoidableType":
            Define inner as cast field-of on (shape, 1).
            // A voidable object can be held behind a pointer, which is a thing in a region.
            If inner's kind is "ObjectType" or inner's kind is "RecordType", return true.
            Return cast one's field-holds-container on (inner, seen).
        Done.
        If kind is "FailureType", return cast one's field-holds-container on (cast field-of on (shape, 1), seen).
        If kind is "UnionType":
            If cast is-open-union on (shape), return true.
            For each member in (cast field-of on (shape, 1))'s children, repeat:
                If cast one's field-holds-container on (member, seen), return true.
            Done.
            Return false.
        Done.
        // A series, a map, a function and its captures, and anything not named above.
        Return true.
    Done.

    /// A store of something that holds a container, met inside a body.
    Bind void to note-store unto checker, given (the node value, the node value-type, the node target, the number at-row):
        If one's store-now is 0, return.
        If cast one's holds-container on (value-type) is false, return.
        Define frame as item (one's store-now) of one's stores's frames.
        Insert (a new store-note { the value value, the target target, the line at-row,
            the sources a series of number, the targets a series of number }) into frame's stores.
    Done.

    /// What ends one argument's places in a cast's flat list of them: no place is this number.
    Bind number to sources-end:
        Return 999999999.
    Done.

    /// Where the `wanted`th argument of a traced cast can come from.
    Bind series of number to argument-sources, given (the call-note noted, the number wanted):
        Define found as a series of number.
        Define reading as 1.
        For each entry-number in noted's given-sources, repeat:
            If entry-number is cast sources-end, increment reading by 1.
            Otherwise if reading is wanted, insert entry-number into found.
        Done.
        Return found.
    Done.

    /// The key what a name's function stores is kept under.
    Bind text to store-key-of unto checker, given (the text written):
        Define pointed as the entry for written in one's stores's held.
        If pointed is not void, return pointed.
        Return written.
    Done.

    /// The frame a name is a function-typed PARAMETER of, looking outward from here — or 0.
    Bind number to function-parameter-frame unto checker, given (the text name):
        Define found as cast one's look-up on (name).
        If found is void, return 0.
        If found's parameter is false or found's shape's kind is not "FunctionType", return 0.
        Define index as one's store-now.
        While index is greater than 0, repeat:
            Define frame as item index of one's stores's frames.
            Define spot as the entry for name in frame's positions.
            If spot is not void:
                If spot is not less than 0, return index.
            Done.
            The index becomes frame's parent.
        Done.
        Return 0.
    Done.

    Bind void to mark-wild unto checker, given (the number frame-index, the text name):
        Define frame as item frame-index of one's stores's frames.
        If frame's summary is "", return.
        Define spot as the entry for name in frame's positions but void is 0.
        Define marked as the entry for frame's summary in one's stores's wild.
        If marked is not void:
            If cast holds-number on (marked, spot) is false, insert spot into marked.
        Done.
    Done.

    Bind text to value-mark, given (the text name, the number at-row, the number at-column):
        Return "{name}\t{at-row}\t{at-column}".
    Done.

    /// A function's name read as a VALUE, not cast. Remembered for the end.
    Bind void to note-function-value unto checker, given (the node said, the binding found):
        If found's shape's kind is not "FunctionType", return.
        Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (said, 1)).
        Define at-row as cast number-of on (cast field-of on (said, 2)).
        Define at-column as cast number-of on (cast field-of on (said, 3)).
        Insert (a new function-value { the stored-as cast one's store-key-of on ("{name}@{found's line}"), the name name,
            the line at-row, the column at-column }) into one's stores's values.
        Define owner as cast one's function-parameter-frame on (name).
        If owner is greater than 0:
            Define frame as item owner of one's stores's frames.
            If frame's summary is not "":
                Insert (a new parameter-value { the owner frame's summary, the slot the entry for name in frame's positions but void is 0,
                    the line at-row, the column at-column }) into one's stores's parameter-values.
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// A function with no name, written where a value goes.
    Bind void to note-lambda-value unto checker, given (the text stored-as, the number at-row, the number at-column):
        Insert (a new function-value { the stored-as stored-as, the name "this function",
            the line at-row, the column at-column }) into one's stores's values.
    Done.

    /// A function written straight into a name, or given a second one: cast by that name, so the
    /// note that it was read as a value is taken back — by where it was READ, not by which
    /// function it is.
    Bind void to hold-function unto checker, given (the text name, the number at-row, the node value):
        Define kind as value's kind.
        If kind is "LambdaLiteral":
            Define at-line as cast number-of on (cast field-of on (value, 3)).
            Define at-column as cast number-of on (cast field-of on (value, 4)).
            In one's stores's taken-back, the entry for cast value-mark on ("this function", at-line, at-column) becomes true.
            In one's stores's held, the entry for "{name}@{at-row}" becomes "lambda@{at-line}:{at-column}".
        Done.
        If kind is "VariableReference":
            Define other as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (value, 1)).
            In one's stores's taken-back, the entry for cast value-mark on (other, cast number-of on (cast field-of on (value, 2)),
                cast number-of on (cast field-of on (value, 3))) becomes true.
            Define found as cast one's look-up on (other).
            If found is not void, in one's stores's held, the entry for "{name}@{at-row}" becomes cast one's store-key-of on ("{other}@{found's line}").
        Done.
    Done.

    /// How deep what an argument names lives: a name's depth whatever its type, or its value's.
    Bind number to place-depth unto checker, given (the node said, the node shape):
        If said's kind is "VariableReference":
            Define found as cast one's look-up on (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (said, 1))).
            If found is not void, return found's depth.
        Done.
        Return cast one's depth-of-value on (said, shape).
    Done.

    /// A cast, once its arguments have been checked. `handed-args` are its arguments without the
    /// object a method is cast on, `receiver` that object or `none`, `callee-key` what its callee's
    /// stores are kept under.
    /// ⚠ No argument is inferred again here: `check-arguments` left each one's type in `memo`.
    /// Inferring them a second time doubles the work at every level of a nested cast.
    Bind void to note-call unto checker, given (the node callee, the text callee-key, the text display,
            the series of node handed-args, the node receiver, the node receiver-type, the number at-row,
            the map from text to node memo):
        Define depths as a series of number.
        Define holds as a series of fact.
        Define shapes as a series of node.
        Define counted as 0.
        For each argument in handed-args, repeat:
            Increment counted by 1.
            Define shape as the entry for "argument {counted}" in memo but void is cast unknown-type.
            Insert shape into shapes.
            Insert cast one's place-depth on (argument, shape) into depths.
            Insert (cast is-reference-type on (shape) or shape's kind is "InterfaceType") into holds.
        Done.
        Define receiver-depth as 0.
        If cast is-none on (receiver) is false, the receiver-depth becomes cast one's place-depth on (receiver, receiver-type).
        Define passes as a series of store-pass.
        Insert (a new call-note { the callee callee-key, the display display, the handed-args handed-args, the receiver receiver,
            the given-depths depths, the given-holds holds, the receiver-depth receiver-depth,
            the call-depth one's rabbit-depth, the line at-row, the within one's store-now,
            the given-sources a series of number, the receiver-sources a series of number,
            the passes passes }) into one's stores's calls.
        If one's store-now is greater than 0:
            Define frame as item (one's store-now) of one's stores's frames.
            Insert the number of one's stores's calls into frame's calls.
        Done.

        // A function parameter cast anywhere but plainly in its own body, outside every rabbit of
        // that body, may be cast deeper than where it was handed over.
        If callee's kind is "VariableReference":
            Define cast-name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (callee, 1)).
            Define cast-owner as cast one's function-parameter-frame on (cast-name).
            If cast-owner is greater than 0:
                If cast-owner is not one's store-now or one's rabbit-depth is greater than 0, cast one's mark-wild on (cast-owner, cast-name).
            Done.
        Done.

        Define place as 0.
        For each argument in handed-args, repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            If (item place of shapes)'s kind is "FunctionType":
                Define kind as argument's kind.
                If kind is "VariableReference":
                    Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (argument, 1)).
                    Define mark as cast value-mark on (name, cast number-of on (cast field-of on (argument, 2)), cast number-of on (cast field-of on (argument, 3))).
                    // Handed over in a cast: judged here, so the note that it was read as a value goes.
                    In one's stores's taken-back, the entry for mark becomes true.
                    Define relayed as cast one's function-parameter-frame on (name).
                    If relayed is greater than 0:
                        In one's stores's taken-back, the entry for "parameter\t{cast number-of on (cast field-of on (argument, 2))}\t{cast number-of on (cast field-of on (argument, 3))}" becomes true.
                        Define owning as item relayed of one's stores's frames.
                        If relayed is one's store-now and one's rabbit-depth is 0:
                            If owning's summary is not "":
                                Define relays as the entry for owning's summary in one's stores's relays.
                                If relays is not void:
                                    Insert (a new store-relay { the slot the entry for name in owning's positions but void is 0,
                                        the toward callee-key, the toward-position place - 1 }) into relays.
                                Done.
                            Done.
                        Done.
                        Otherwise, cast one's mark-wild on (relayed, name).
                    Done.
                    Otherwise:
                        Define found as cast one's look-up on (name).
                        If found is not void:
                            Insert (a new store-pass { the slot place - 1, the handed cast one's store-key-of on ("{name}@{found's line}") }) into passes.
                        Done.
                    Done.
                Done.
                If kind is "LambdaLiteral":
                    Define at-line as cast number-of on (cast field-of on (argument, 3)).
                    Define at-column as cast number-of on (cast field-of on (argument, 4)).
                    In one's stores's taken-back, the entry for cast value-mark on ("this function", at-line, at-column) becomes true.
                    Insert (a new store-pass { the slot place - 1, the handed "lambda@{at-line}:{at-column}" }) into passes.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.

    // ── Judging, once every body has been checked ─────────────────────────

    /// The names of every object that says it is this interface.
    Bind series of text to conformers unto checker, given (the text interface-name):
        Define found as a series of text.
        For each name in one's def-order, repeat:
            Define definition as cast one's definition-of on (name).
            If definition is not void:
                For each conformed in cast conformed-names on (definition), repeat:
                    If conformed is interface-name, insert name into found.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
        Return found.
    Done.

    /// The keys an interface's method stands for: every conforming object's own.
    Bind series of text to behind-key unto checker, given (the text stored-as):
        Define keys as a series of text.
        If stored-as starts with "interface\t" is false:
            Insert stored-as into keys.
            Return keys.
        Done.
        Define parts as stored-as split by "\t".
        Define interface-name as item 2 of parts.
        Define method-name as item 3 of parts.
        For each owner in cast one's conformers on (interface-name), repeat:
            If cast one's method-type-of on (owner, method-name) is not void:
                Insert "{cast one's method-owner on (owner, method-name)}'s {method-name}" into keys.
            Done.
        Done.
        Return keys.
    Done.

    /// What a function stores, in order.
    Bind series of store-pair to pairs-of unto checker, given (the text stored-as):
        Define all-pairs as a series of store-pair.
        For each one-key in cast one's behind-key on (stored-as), repeat:
            Define kept as the entry for one-key in one's stores's pairs.
            If kept is not void:
                For each one-pair in kept, repeat:
                    If cast holds-pair on (all-pairs, one-pair's from-place, one-pair's into-place) is false, insert one-pair into all-pairs.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
        Return cast pairs-in-order on (all-pairs).
    Done.

    /// Whether a function may cast this parameter of its own deeper than it was handed it.
    Bind fact to is-wild unto checker, given (the text stored-as, the number slot):
        If stored-as starts with "interface\t":
            For each one-key in cast one's behind-key on (stored-as), repeat:
                If cast one's is-wild on (one-key, slot), return true.
            Done.
            Return false.
        Done.
        If (the entry for stored-as in one's stores's known) is void, return true.
        Define marked as the entry for stored-as in one's stores's wild.
        If marked is void, return false.
        Return cast holds-number on (marked, slot).
    Done.

    Bind fact to captures-names unto checker, given (the text stored-as):
        Return (the entry for stored-as in one's stores's captures but void is false).
    Done.

    /// The frame a function was written in — 0 at the top level, -1 when nothing was written.
    Bind number to written-in unto checker, given (the text stored-as):
        Return (the entry for stored-as in one's stores's defined-in but void is -1).
    Done.

    /// A captured place of some function, in the terms of the body that casts or hands it.
    Bind series of number to captured-place unto checker, given (the number frame-index, the text stored-as, the number place):
        If place is cast outer-unknown, return a series with (place).
        Define frame as item frame-index of one's stores's frames.
        Define written as cast one's written-in on (stored-as).
        // Written in this body: the name is one of this body's own, a parameter or made here.
        If written is frame-index:
            If cast is-outer-parameter on (place), return a series with (cast outer-parameter-base - place).
            Return a series with (-2).
        Done.
        // Written beside this body: the same name, captured by both, the same way.
        If written is frame's parent, return a series with (place).
        Return a series with (cast outer-unknown).
    Done.

    /// Everything the receiver of a cast could cast a function it is handed on, in the terms of
    /// the body making the cast.
    Bind series of number to receiver-reach unto checker, given (the number frame-index, the call-note noted):
        Define frame as item frame-index of one's stores's frames.
        Define reach as a series with (-2).
        Define place as 0.
        For each holding in noted's given-holds, repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            If holding, cast union-into on (cast argument-sources on (noted, place), reach).
        Done.
        If cast is-none on (noted's receiver) is false, cast union-into on (noted's receiver-sources, reach).
        If cast one's captures-names on (noted's callee):
            Define written as cast one's written-in on (noted's callee).
            // What the receiver captured. Written in this body, those are this body's names.
            If written is frame-index, cast union-into on (cast untraced on (frame's referenced, a map from text to number), reach).
            Otherwise if written is frame's parent:
                For each pair in frame's captured, repeat:
                    If cast holds-number on (reach, the value of pair) is false, insert the value of pair into reach.
                Done.
            Done.
            Otherwise if cast holds-number on (reach, cast outer-unknown) is false, insert cast outer-unknown into reach.
        Done.
        Return reach.
    Done.

    /// One store a body makes, by its own hand or through a function it casts: where it may come
    /// from, where it may go, and how to say it.
    Define object store-event with (the series of number sources, the series of number targets, the number line, the text by-way-of).

    Bind series of store-event to stores-of unto checker, given (the number frame-index):
        Define frame as item frame-index of one's stores's frames.
        Define events as a series of store-event.
        If the number of frame's stores is greater than 0, cast one's trace-frame on (frame-index).
        For each store in frame's stores, repeat:
            Insert (a new store-event { the sources store's sources, the targets store's targets, the line store's line, the by-way-of "" }) into events.
        Done.
        For each call-index in frame's calls, repeat:
            Define noted as item call-index of one's stores's calls.
            Define stored as cast one's pairs-of on (noted's callee).
            If the number of stored is greater than 0:
                Cast one's trace-frame on (frame-index).
                For each one-pair in stored, repeat:
                    Define sources as cast one's place-sources on (frame-index, noted, noted's callee, one-pair's from-place).
                    Define targets as cast one's place-sources on (frame-index, noted, noted's callee, one-pair's into-place).
                    If sources is not void and targets is not void:
                        Insert (a new store-event { the sources sources, the targets targets, the line noted's line, the by-way-of noted's display }) into events.
                    Done.
                Done.
            Done.
            // A function handed over here, judged as though it were cast here on anything the
            // receiver could cast it on.
            For each handing in noted's passes, repeat:
                Define handed-pairs as cast one's pairs-of on (handing's handed).
                If the number of handed-pairs is greater than 0:
                    Cast one's trace-frame on (frame-index).
                    Define reach as cast one's receiver-reach on (frame-index, noted).
                    For each one-pair in handed-pairs, repeat:
                        Insert (a new store-event {
                            the sources cast one's handed-side on (frame-index, handing's handed, one-pair's from-place, reach),
                            the targets cast one's handed-side on (frame-index, handing's handed, one-pair's into-place, reach),
                            the line noted's line, the by-way-of "the function handed to {noted's display}" }) into events.
                    Done.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
        Return events.
    Done.

    Bind series of number to handed-side unto checker, given (the number frame-index, the text stored-as, the number place, the series of number reach):
        If place is -2, return a series with (-2).
        If cast is-outer on (place) is false, return reach.
        Return cast one's captured-place on (frame-index, stored-as, place).
    Done.

    /// What one side of a callee's pair is, in the terms of the body making the cast — or void.
    Bind voidable series of number to place-sources unto checker, given (the number frame-index, the call-note noted,
            the text stored-as, the number place):
        If place is -2, return a series with (-2).
        If place is -1:
            If cast is-none on (noted's receiver), return void.
            Return noted's receiver-sources.
        Done.
        If place is not less than 0:
            If place is less than the number of noted's handed-args, return cast argument-sources on (noted, place + 1).
            Return void.
        Done.
        Return cast one's captured-place on (frame-index, stored-as, place).
    Done.

    /// 0: nothing to say. 1: a pair of this body's. 2: refused.
    Bind number to store-verdict, given (the store-frame frame, the number from-place, the number into-place):
        If from-place is into-place or into-place is -2, return 0.
        If from-place is cast outer-unknown or into-place is cast outer-unknown, return 2.
        // Both captured, at depths known in the body: `check-region-store` judged them there. With
        // a parameter of the body around on either side it is that body's pair, like any other.
        If cast is-outer on (from-place) and cast is-outer on (into-place)
                and cast is-outer-parameter on (from-place) is false and cast is-outer-parameter on (into-place) is false:
            Return 0.
        Done.
        If frame's summary is not "", return 1.
        // The one store a setter is FOR is checked where the field is set, as the store it is.
        If frame's setter and from-place is 0 and into-place is -1, return 1.
        Return 2.
    Done.

    Bind text to place-name, given (the number place):
        If place is -2, return "something it makes".
        If place is -1, return "the object it is cast on".
        If cast is-outer on (place), return "a name from outside it".
        Return "argument {place + 1}".
    Done.

    Bind text to refused-in-body, given (the number from-place, the number into-place, the number at-row, the text by-way-of):
        Define doing as "this stores".
        If by-way-of is not "", the doing becomes "this casts {by-way-of}, which stores".
        If cast is-outer on (from-place) or cast is-outer on (into-place):
            Return cast refusal-of on (
                "{doing} between what this function was given or made and a name from outside it, and nothing here can say which of the two lives longer",
                "That name is a parameter of the function around this one, or comes from further out than that",
                at-row, "store where the value may not live long enough",
                "Pass the container in as a parameter, or give the value back with 'Return' and store it where the function is cast.").
        Done.
        Return cast refusal-of on (
            "{doing} a series or an object into something it was given, where no cast can be checked",
            "A getter, a setter, an operator and an unmaker are not cast, so there is no call to check what they store against",
            at-row, "store into what it was given",
            "Do the storing in a method, and cast that.").
    Done.

    /// The depth one side of a callee's pair has where it is cast, or -1 when there is none to give.
    Bind number to depth-at-call unto checker, given (the call-note noted, the number place):
        If place is -2, return noted's call-depth.
        If place is -1:
            If cast is-none on (noted's receiver), return -1.
            Return noted's receiver-depth.
        Done.
        If place is not less than 0:
            If place is less than the number of noted's given-depths, return item (place + 1) of noted's given-depths.
            Return -1.
        Done.
        // A captured depth means something only in the body the callee was written in.
        If cast one's written-in on (noted's callee) is noted's within and place is not cast outer-unknown, return cast outer-depth on (place).
        Return -1.
    Done.

    Bind void or failure to refuse-at-call unto checker, given (the call-note noted, the number from-place, the number into-place):
        Define coming as cast one's depth-at-call on (noted, from-place).
        Define going as cast one's depth-at-call on (noted, into-place).
        If coming is less than 0 or going is less than 0 or coming is not greater than going, return.
        Define said as "This cast reaches {noted's display}, which stores {cast place-name on (from-place)} into {cast place-name on (into-place)}".
        Define action as "cast it with a value from a shorter-lived region than the container".
        If from-place is -2:
            The said becomes "{said}, and what a function makes lives in the region it is cast in".
            The action becomes "cast it inside a region, on a container from outside that region".
        Done.
        Return a failure (cast refusal-of on (
            "this value lives in a shorter-lived region than its destination — it will be gone when that region ends",
            said, noted's line, action,
            "Declare the container inside that region too, so both end at its 'Done.', or cast it before the region opens.")).
    Done.

    Bind void or failure to refuse-at-pass unto checker, given (the call-note noted, the store-pass handing):
        Define stored as cast one's pairs-of on (handing's handed).
        If the number of stored is 0, return.
        If cast one's is-wild on (noted's callee, handing's slot):
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on (
                "this function stores into what it is given or what is around it, and it is handed to something that may cast it in a shorter-lived region",
                "It is handed to {noted's display}, which casts the function it is given inside a rabbit of its own, or keeps it, or has no body to read",
                noted's line, "hand it over as argument {handing's slot + 1}",
                "Hand over a function that gives its result back with 'Return', and store the result here.")).
        Done.
        // As though cast here: what it makes is as deep as this cast, and what it is given is as
        // deep as this cast or as any container handed over beside it.
        Define written as cast one's written-in on (handing's handed) is noted's within.
        Define deepest as noted's call-depth.
        Define shallowest as noted's call-depth.
        Define place as 0.
        For each depth in noted's given-depths, repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            If item place of noted's given-holds:
                If depth is greater than deepest, the deepest becomes depth.
                If depth is less than shallowest, the shallowest becomes depth.
            Done.
        Done.
        If cast is-none on (noted's receiver) is false:
            If noted's receiver-depth is greater than deepest, the deepest becomes noted's receiver-depth.
            If noted's receiver-depth is less than shallowest, the shallowest becomes noted's receiver-depth.
        Done.
        // What the receiver captured is no deeper than where the receiver was written.
        If cast one's captures-names on (noted's callee), the shallowest becomes 0.

        For each one-pair in stored, repeat:
            If one-pair's into-place is not -2:
                // -1: nothing to compare.
                Define from-deepest as deepest.
                If one-pair's from-place is -2, the from-deepest becomes noted's call-depth.
                If cast is-outer on (one-pair's from-place):
                    The from-deepest becomes -1.
                    If written and one-pair's from-place is not cast outer-unknown, the from-deepest becomes cast outer-depth on (one-pair's from-place).
                Done.
                Define into-shallowest as shallowest.
                If cast is-outer on (one-pair's into-place):
                    The into-shallowest becomes -1.
                    If written and one-pair's into-place is not cast outer-unknown, the into-shallowest becomes cast outer-depth on (one-pair's into-place).
                Done.
                If from-deepest is not less than 0 and into-shallowest is not less than 0 and from-deepest is greater than into-shallowest:
                    Return a failure (cast refusal-of on (
                        "this value lives in a shorter-lived region than its destination — it will be gone when that region ends",
                        "The function handed to {noted's display} stores {cast place-name on (one-pair's from-place)} into {cast place-name on (one-pair's into-place)}, and {noted's display} can cast it on anything it is given here or makes here",
                        noted's line,
                        "hand it over as argument {handing's slot + 1}, inside a region, with a container from outside that region in reach",
                        "Declare the container inside that region too, so both end at its 'Done.', or make the cast before the region opens.")).
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// Whether a function stores anything at all — asked before any list is built, since most do not.
    Bind fact to stores-anything unto checker, given (the text stored-as):
        If stored-as starts with "interface\t":
            For each one-key in cast one's behind-key on (stored-as), repeat:
                If cast one's stores-anything on (one-key), return true.
            Done.
            Return false.
        Done.
        Define kept as the entry for stored-as in one's stores's pairs.
        If kept is void, return false.
        Return the number of kept is greater than 0.
    Done.

    /// Whether a body has any store to judge: one of its own, a cast of a function that stores, or
    /// a function that stores handed over. ⚠ Most bodies have none, and nothing is built for them:
    /// over a large program the lists built for every body were a sixth of the checker's memory.
    Bind fact to has-stores unto checker, given (the store-frame frame):
        If the number of frame's stores is greater than 0, return true.
        For each call-index in frame's calls, repeat:
            Define noted as item call-index of one's stores's calls.
            If cast one's stores-anything on (noted's callee), return true.
            For each handing in noted's passes, repeat:
                If cast one's stores-anything on (handing's handed), return true.
            Done.
        Done.
        Return false.
    Done.

    /// `CheckStoresAtCalls`: every body has been checked, so what each function stores is known
    /// whatever order they were written in.
    Bind void or failure to judge-stores unto checker:
        // A function parameter read as a value and not simply handed on is kept somewhere.
        For each noticed in one's stores's parameter-values, repeat:
            If (the entry for "parameter\t{noticed's line}\t{noticed's column}" in one's stores's taken-back) is void:
                Define marked as the entry for noticed's owner in one's stores's wild.
                If marked is not void:
                    If cast holds-number on (marked, noticed's slot) is false, insert noticed's slot into marked.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.

        // What each body stores, to a fixed point: a function that hands its parameter on to one
        // that stores into it stores into it too. The same for a function parameter handed on to a
        // function that casts it deeper.
        Define changed as true.
        While changed, repeat:
            The changed becomes false.
            For each frame-index in one's stores's closed, repeat:
                Define frame as item frame-index of one's stores's frames.
                If frame's summary is not "":
                    Define relays as the entry for frame's summary in one's stores's relays.
                    Define marked as the entry for frame's summary in one's stores's wild.
                    If relays is not void and marked is not void:
                        For each relay in relays, repeat:
                            If cast one's is-wild on (relay's toward, relay's toward-position) and cast holds-number on (marked, relay's slot) is false:
                                Insert relay's slot into marked.
                                The changed becomes true.
                            Done.
                        Done.
                    Done.
                Done.
            Done.
            For each frame-index in one's stores's closed, repeat:
                Define frame as item frame-index of one's stores's frames.
                If frame's summary is not "" and cast one's has-stores on (frame):
                    Define kept as the entry for frame's summary in one's stores's pairs.
                    If kept is not void:
                        For each event in cast one's stores-of on (frame-index), repeat:
                            For each from-place in cast places-in-order on (event's sources), repeat:
                                For each into-place in cast places-in-order on (event's targets), repeat:
                                    If cast store-verdict on (frame, from-place, into-place) is 1:
                                        If cast holds-pair on (kept, from-place, into-place) is false:
                                            Insert (a new store-pair { the from-place from-place, the into-place into-place }) into kept.
                                            The changed becomes true.
                                        Done.
                                    Done.
                                Done.
                            Done.
                        Done.
                    Done.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.

        For each frame-index in one's stores's closed, repeat:
            Define frame as item frame-index of one's stores's frames.
            If cast one's has-stores on (frame):
                For each event in cast one's stores-of on (frame-index), repeat:
                    For each from-place in cast places-in-order on (event's sources), repeat:
                        For each into-place in cast places-in-order on (event's targets), repeat:
                            If cast store-verdict on (frame, from-place, into-place) is 2:
                                Return a failure (cast refused-in-body on (from-place, into-place, event's line, event's by-way-of)).
                            Done.
                        Done.
                    Done.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.

        For each noticed in one's stores's values, repeat:
            If (the entry for cast value-mark on (noticed's name, noticed's line, noticed's column) in one's stores's taken-back) is void:
                If cast one's stores-anything on (noticed's stored-as):
                    Define naming as "'{noticed's name}'".
                    If noticed's name is "this function", the naming becomes noticed's name.
                    Return a failure (cast refusal-of on (
                        "{naming} stores into what it is given or what is around it, so it cannot be handed on as a value",
                        "Each cast of it is checked against what it stores, and a cast through a value does not say which function it reaches",
                        noticed's line, "keep it where nothing can follow it",
                        "Hold it in a name with 'Define' and cast it by that name, or hand it straight to the function that casts it.")).
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.

        For each noted in one's stores's calls, repeat:
            If cast one's stores-anything on (noted's callee):
                For each one-pair in cast one's pairs-of on (noted's callee), repeat:
                    Cast one's refuse-at-call on (noted, one-pair's from-place, one-pair's into-place) or pass the failure off.
                Done.
            Done.
            For each handing in noted's passes, repeat:
                If cast one's stores-anything on (handing's handed):
                    Cast one's refuse-at-pass on (noted, handing) or pass the failure off.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.
Done.
